<title>PHILIPPINES: Taiwanese firm buys stake in new Philippine bank.</title>
<headline>Taiwanese firm buys stake in new Philippine bank.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's China United Trust and Investment Corp had bought 30 percent in a newly formed bank called Asia Pacific Banking Corp, the Central Bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank is majority owned by Republic Biscuit Corp, a local biscuit manufacturer.</p>
<p>The newly-approved bank has an authorised capital stock of five billion pesos, of which 1.25 billion pesos have been subscribed.</p>
<p>Asia Pacific Bank is the 51st commercial bank to operate in the country. - Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
